# Process, terminal, and preview cleanup

## On demand only (default: off)

These are **not** part of every task. Use them only when the **user explicitly asks**:

- Browser MCP / built-in browser automation
- Integrated terminal (shell commands, background jobs)
- Dev server (`npm run dev`, `npm run dev:fast`, `dev-server/start-restart-dev.bat`)

When the user asks, run what they requested, complete it, and clean up afterward.

## Mandatory cleanup

- If the agent started a background terminal command or dev server (because the user asked), stop that shell/process when the task is done or before ending the chat
- Do not leave agent-started `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, or similar running after the task completes

## Never kill or stop (user-owned)

- The user's browser (Edge, Chrome, Firefox, etc.)
- Processes started by `dev-server/start-restart-dev.bat` or `dev-server/stop-dev.bat`
- Broad kills (`taskkill node`, close all terminals, kill port 4321) unless the user explicitly asks

## End-of-task reminder (visual / preview work)

After layout, scroll, or animation changes — unless the user asked you to verify in browser — add one short reminder:

> Close your preview browser tab or run `dev-server/stop-dev.bat` when done.

Do not run `stop-dev.bat` or kill preview processes yourself unless the user asks.

## RAM discipline

- Default: edit source only; no terminal, dev server, or browser unless the user requests on demand
- User may preview locally outside Cursor or provide screenshots
